.Dd April 30, 2026
.Dt EMU.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm emu.conf
.Nd FreeBSD emulation framework configuration file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file contains configuration settings for the
.Fx
emulation framework.
It uses a simple
.Va key=value
format with one setting per line.
Lines starting with
.Ql #
or empty lines are treated as comments and ignored.
.Pp
The configuration file supports both system-wide and per-user settings:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
System-wide configuration (set during installation)
.It Pa ~/.config/emu/emu.conf
Per-user configuration (overrides system settings)
.El
.Pp
Settings in the per-user configuration file override the system-wide
defaults.
.Sh CONFIGURATION OPTIONS
The following configuration options are supported:
.Ss Instance Management
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va instance_dir No = Ar path
Directory for storing emulation instance data.
The default is
.Pa /var/emu .
.It Va image_cache_dir No = Ar path
Directory for caching emulation disk images.
The default is
.Pa /var/cache/emu/images .
.El
.Ss Default Instance Settings
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va default_arch No = Ar arch
Default target architecture for new instances.
.Ar arch
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "amd64" -compact
.It amd64
x86-64 (64-bit)
.It i386
x86 (32-bit)
.It arm64
AArch64 (64-bit ARM)
.It arm
ARM (32-bit)
.It powerpc
PowerPC
.It riscv
RISC-V (64-bit)
.El
The default is
.Va amd64 .
.It Va default_mode No = Ar mode
Default execution mode.
.Ar mode
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "auto" -compact
.It auto
Automatically select best mode based on architecture
.It bhyve
Use bhyve/VMM virtualization (native architectures only)
.It emulator
Use custom software emulator
.El
The default is
.Va auto .
.It Va default_cpu_level No = Ar level
Default CPU compatibility level.
.Ar level
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "x86-64-v3" -compact
.It 1
Base compatibility level
.It 2
Extended features (SSE4, POPCOUNT)
.It 3
Maximum features (AVX2, BMI2)
.El
The meaning varies by architecture.
.It Va default_cpu_speed_mhz No = Ar speed
Default CPU speed in MHz.
Use
.Va 0
for auto-detection.
The default is
.Va 0 .
.It Va default_memory No = Ar size
Default memory size for new instances.
.Ar size
can be specified with optional suffix:
.Bl -tag -width "512M" -compact
.It 256M
256 megabytes
.It 1G
1 gigabyte
.It 2G
2 gigabytes
.El
The default is
.Va 256M .
.It Va default_cpus No = Ar count
Default number of virtual CPUs.
The default is
.Va 1 .
.El
.Ss Output Settings
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va output_format No = Ar format
Default output format for commands.
.Ar format
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "json" -compact
.It text
Human-readable text output (default)
.It json
JSON output for machine parsing
.It tap
Test Anything Protocol
.It junit
JUnit XML format
.El
.It Va verbose No = Ar value
Enable verbose output.
.Ar value
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "yes" -compact
.It yes
Enable verbose output
.It true
Enable verbose output
.It 1
Enable verbose output
.El
The default is
.Va no .
.El
.Ss Security Settings
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va securelevel No = Ar level
Kernel securelevel for emulation instances.
.Ar level
can be:
.Bl -tag -width "-1" -compact
.It -1
Permanently insecure (never raise)
.It 0
Insecure (default for development)
.It 1
Secure (default for production)
.It 2
Highly secure
.It 3
Network-secure (maximum)
.El
.It Va mac_enforce No = Ar bool
Enable MAC label enforcement.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va veriexec_check No = Ar bool
Verify binary integrity via veriexec.
The default is
.Va auto
(detect if available).
.It Va audit_enabled No = Ar bool
Enable security auditing for emulation events.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va audit_buffer_size No = Ar size
Audit event buffer size (number of events).
The default is
.Va 1024 .
.It Va memory_encryption No = Ar bool
Enable memory encryption for instances.
Requires CPU AES-NI.
The default is
.Va false .
.It Va balloon_enabled No = Ar bool
Enable memory balloon driver for instances.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va balloon_target_pages No = Ar count
Target pages for memory balloon adjustment.
The default is
.Va 256
(1MB on amd64).
.It Va balloon_interval_secs No = Ar seconds
Interval between balloon adjustments.
The default is
.Va 5 .
.El
.Ss Resource Limits
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va max_instances No = Ar count
Maximum number of concurrent emulation instances.
The default is
.Va 32 .
.It Va max_memory_mb No = Ar size
Maximum total memory for all instances (MB).
The default is
.Va 65536
(64GB).
.It Va max_vcpus No = Ar count
Maximum virtual CPUs per instance.
The default is
.Va 16 .
.It Va memory_warn_percent No = Ar percent
Warn when system memory usage exceeds this percentage.
The default is
.Va 85 .
.It Va oom_protection No = Ar bool
Enable OOM protection for emulator processes.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va rctl_enabled No = Ar bool
Enable resource limits via rctl subsystem.
The default is
.Va auto .
.El
.Ss Network Security
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va network_isolation No = Ar bool
Isolate emulation network from host network.
The default is
.Va false .
.It Va network_nat No = Ar bool
Use NAT for emulation network access.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va firewall_rules No = Ar path
Path to custom firewall rules file.
.Disabled by default.
.It Va vmm_strict_priority No = Ar bool
Give emulator processes strict priority.
The default is
.Va true .
.El
.Ss Snapshot and Share Security
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va snapshot_require_mac No = Ar bool
Require matching MAC labels for snapshots.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va share_require_mac No = Ar bool
Require matching MAC labels for file shares.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va share_path_validation No = Ar bool
Validate shared paths are within allowed directories.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va snapshot_allowed_dirs No = Ar path
Comma-separated list of allowed snapshot directories.
Default is
.Va /var/emu/snapshots .
.El
.Ss Kernel Module Options
.Bl -tag -width Fl -compact
.It Va module_debug No = Ar bool
Enable kernel module debug logging.
The default is
.Va false .
.It Va module_audit_level No = Ar level
Kernel audit level (0=off, 1=errors, 2=warnings, 3=info, 4=debug).
The default is
.Va 1 .
.It Va conflict_check No = Ar bool
Check for conflicting virtualization modules.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va numa_aware No = Ar bool
Enable NUMA-aware memory allocation.
The default is
.Va true .
.It Va huge_pages No = Ar bool
Attempt to use huge pages for instance memory.
The default is
.Va auto .
.It Va swap_encryption No = Ar bool
Encrypt swap pages for instance memory.
The default is
.Va false .
.It Va cpu_affinity No = Ar list
Comma-separated list of CPUs for emulator affinity.
.Disabled by default.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/emu/emu.conf
System-wide configuration file
.It Pa ~/.config/emu/emu.conf
Per-user configuration file
.It Pa /var/emu/
Default instance data directory
.It Pa /var/cache/emu/images/
Default image cache directory
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss Basic Development Configuration (Insecure)
This configuration is suitable for local development where security is not a concern.
All security features are disabled for maximum performance and debugging capability.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# emu.conf - Basic Development Configuration
# WARNING: This configuration is INSECURE and should only be used
# in isolated development environments.

# Disable all security features
securelevel=-1
mac_enforce=false
veriexec_check=false
audit_enabled=false

# Disable resource limits
max_instances=128
max_memory_mb=131072
oom_protection=false
rctl_enabled=false

# Disable network security
network_isolation=false
network_nat=true
vmm_strict_priority=false

# Disable snapshot/share security
snapshot_require_mac=false
share_require_mac=false
share_path_validation=false

# Debug everything
module_debug=true
module_audit_level=4

# Performance over security
balloon_enabled=true
memory_encryption=false
swap_encryption=false
.Ed
.Pp
.Ss Standard Configuration
This configuration balances security and usability for general purpose emulation.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# emu.conf - Standard Configuration
# Balanced security for general use

# Standard security settings
securelevel=1
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
audit_buffer_size=2048

# Resource limits
max_instances=32
max_memory_mb=65536
max_vcpus=16
memory_warn_percent=85
oom_protection=true
rctl_enabled=true

# Network security
network_isolation=false
network_nat=true
vmm_strict_priority=true

# Snapshot/share security
snapshot_require_mac=true
share_require_mac=true
share_path_validation=true

# Debug disabled
module_debug=false
module_audit_level=1

# Memory management
balloon_enabled=true
memory_encryption=false
swap_encryption=false
numa_aware=true
huge_pages=auto
.Ed
.Pp
.Ss High Security Configuration
This configuration provides enhanced security for sensitive workloads.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# emu.conf - High Security Configuration
# Enhanced security for sensitive workloads

# Maximum security
securelevel=3
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
audit_buffer_size=8192

# Strict resource limits
max_instances=16
max_memory_mb=32768
max_vcpus=8
memory_warn_percent=75
oom_protection=true
rctl_enabled=true

# Network isolation
network_isolation=true
network_nat=true
vmm_strict_priority=true

# Strict snapshot/share security
snapshot_require_mac=true
share_require_mac=true
share_path_validation=true
snapshot_allowed_dirs=/var/emu/snapshots,/secure/emu/snapshots

# Kernel hardening
module_debug=false
module_audit_level=2
conflict_check=true
numa_aware=true
huge_pages=true
swap_encryption=true

# Memory encryption if available
memory_encryption=true
.Ed
.Pp
.Ss Maximum Security Configuration
This configuration provides the highest level of security for critical infrastructure.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# emu.conf - Maximum Security Configuration
# WARNING: Requires significant system configuration

# Lock down security
securelevel=3
mac_enforce=true
veriexec_check=true
audit_enabled=true
audit_buffer_size=16384

# Minimal resource limits
max_instances=8
max_memory_mb=16384
max_vcpus=4
memory_warn_percent=60
oom_protection=true
rctl_enabled=true

# Complete network isolation
network_isolation=true
network_nat=true
vmm_strict_priority=true
firewall_rules=/etc/emu/firewall.rules

# Maximum snapshot/share restrictions
snapshot_require_mac=true
share_require_mac=true
share_path_validation=true
snapshot_allowed_dirs=/secure/emu/snapshots

# Kernel hardening
module_debug=false
module_audit_level=3
conflict_check=true
numa_aware=true
huge_pages=true
swap_encryption=true
cpu_affinity=0,1,2,3

# Memory encryption
memory_encryption=true
balloon_enabled=false
.Ed
.Pp
.Ss Instance Directories
Configure instance and cache directories:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Instance directories
instance_dir=/var/emu
image_cache_dir=/var/cache/emu/images

# Default settings for new instances
default_arch=amd64
default_mode=auto
default_memory=512M
default_cpus=2

# CPU compatibility level (1-3)
default_cpu_level=2

# Output format (text, json, tap, junit)
output_format=text

# Enable verbose output (yes, true, or 1)
verbose=no
.Ed
.Pp
To use arm64 as the default architecture:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
default_arch=arm64
default_memory=1G
default_cpus=4
.Ed
.Sh HOST CONFIGURATION
This section describes how to configure the host system for each security level.
.Ss Enabling MAC Veriexec
To enable veriexec binary verification:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /boot/loader.conf
mac_veriexec_load="YES"

# Create veriexec manifest in /etc/veriexec
# See veriexecctl(8) for manifest format
.Ed
.Ss Enabling Securelevel
To set the kernel securelevel:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /etc/rc.conf
kern_securelevel_enable="YES"
kern_securelevel="1"
.Ed
.Ss Enabling rctl Resource Limits
To enable rctl resource control:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /etc/rc.conf
jail_enable="YES"
rctl_enable="YES"

# Add resource limits in /etc/rctl.conf
# user:emu:maxproc=100
# user:emu:memoryuse=4G
.Ed
.Ss Enabling Huge Pages
To enable huge pages for instance memory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Add to /etc/sysctl.conf
vm.pmap.pg_ps_enabled=1

# Configure huge pages (requires reboot)
# Add to /boot/loader.conf
vm.hmem_size=8G
vm.pmap.pg_ps__enabled=1
.Ed
.Ss Configuring Network Isolation
To configure isolated network for emulation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# Create isolated bridge
# Add to /etc/rc.conf
cloned_interfaces="bridge0"
ifconfig_bridge0="addm emu0 up"
.Ed
